The obvious reason is that males and females do have similar densities in your population - and you haven't really produced evidence that they don't. If you want a more specific answer please provide detail (data or data summary and code). If you use the 'hcov' route for modelling sex-specific detection and sex ratio then exactly the same total density is reported for males and females.
Murray

